# AdPilot environment variables.
# Copy to .env.local (never commit it) and fill in only what you have.
# EVERY variable is optional: with none of them AdPilot still returns a full plan
# from the trained XGBoost scorer, the India 2026 rate card, the festival calendar,
# the site checks and copy templates. Keys are read on the server only.
# On Vercel: Project > Settings > Environment Variables (see docs/PUSH-CHECKLIST.md).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM wording (English only). Never changes scores, rupees or numbers.
# Launch-kit rewrite + ad copy: Gemini first, Groq as fallback (on failure,
# timeout, unusable JSON or an echo of the input). Product recognition: Groq first.
# OpenAI is not used.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# console.groq.com > API Keys (free tier).
GROQ_API_KEY=
# Optional model override. Llama models are Enterprise-only on Groq now.
# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b

# aistudio.google.com > Get API key.
GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=
# Optional model override (gemini-2.0-flash is shut down).
# GOOGLE_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Storage. Without this, plans live in server memory + browser localStorage and
# the API cache is an in-memory Map. JSON files are not used: they do not
# persist on Vercel serverless. Creates adpilot_plans, adpilot_rate_card and
# adpilot_cache on first use.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vercel > Storage > Postgres (Neon), or neon.tech. Injected automatically on Vercel.
POSTGRES_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Offline mode. Set to 1 to make every data source read
# fixtures/api/<source>/*.json instead of calling live APIs (demo, tests, eval).
# Local/dev only: fixture files are not bundled into Vercel functions,
# so never set this on Vercel.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ADPILOT_MOCK_APIS=
# Optional: read mock fixtures from another folder (tests use this).
# ADPILOT_FIXTURE_DIR=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v2 data sources (each unlocks one dashboard card; without it the card says
# "Not connected"). Restrict every Google key to its one API.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# F1 part B: PageSpeed Insights v5 (mobile speed, checked after the plan renders,
# cached 24h). Google Cloud > enable "PageSpeed Insights API" > API key
# restricted to that API. Free.
PAGESPEED_API_KEY=

# F2: Google Places API (New), Text Search (local competitors + "are you on Maps?",
# cached 7 days). Needs billing on the Cloud project. Restrict the key to
# Places API (New) and set a daily quota + budget alert. Rating fields put
# competitor search on the Enterprise SKU.
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=

# F5: YouTube Data API v3 (local creator finder). Same Cloud project > enable
# "YouTube Data API v3" > key restricted to it. Free: 10,000 units/day; one plan
# costs 101 units (search.list 100 + channels.list 1), cached 7 days.
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=

# F4: Meta audience size (Marketing API reachestimate). Server-side system-user
# token with ads_read; no user OAuth, no spend. All three are needed; without them
# the "Who you can reach" chapter says Not connected. Verify with:
#   npm run record -- meta
META_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# Ad account id, with or without the act_ prefix.
META_AD_ACCOUNT_ID=
# Pinned Graph/Marketing API version, e.g. v26.0 (latest as of Jul 2026).
META_API_VERSION=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not used yet (future work, M6). Listed so the roadmap and env stay in sync;
# setting them has no effect today.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# F6 search demand (Google Trends via SerpAPI), serpapi.com.
# SERPAPI_API_KEY=
# F3 festival cross-check, calendarific.com.
# CALENDARIFIC_API_KEY=
